htr3_new.c's search in Capla, and its proof
===========================================

run/        the program and how to check a table file with it (no Rocq):
            see run/README.
proof/      the Rocq proofs on Capla's semantics (opam switch capla, Rocq 9.0;
            Capla configured with -use-external-Flocq).  `make -C proof all`.
            HtrFinal.v, search_complete: on a line whose array holds
            P(0) .. P(K-1) mod beta^L, under the hypotheses of hscan_exp
            (H_A, H_T, H_E), every hard j < N is among the candidates that
            search returns, when their number is at most cap.  It rests on
            WP_sound, ADMITTED in Capla itself (bfrontend/WP.v), on Capla's
            external_functions_sem and on the standard axioms.
            HtrTable.v links it to the table check through line_ok
            (code/exptablekl/ExpCheck.v), where each line has its own
            number of terms k and of words l: search_line, on a line
            with line_ok, every j < n whose input (S0 + j) 2^(ex - 52) is
            hard (code/exptablekl/ExpHard.v) is among the candidates that
            search returns, run with the k and l of the line and
            err = ERR = 0x600000, when their number is at most cap;
            search_table: check_raw ls = true gives, for every line of
            ls, its parse (S0, ex, n, k, l, B), line_ok and the
            conclusion of search_line.  The chain: check_raw -> line_ok
            -> no hard input missed.  search_line has the assumptions of
            search_complete; search_table adds the primitive integers
            and strings used by the check (PrimInt63, Uint63Axioms,
            PrimString).
apaul/,     links to code/APaul/rocq, code/exptable9 and code/exptablekl,
exptable9/, compiled here in the switch capla (`make -C proof ports`).
exptablekl/

For rocq-mcp, `make -C proof mcp` links Capla's libraries into caplalib/
and writes _CoqProject (both local); the workspace is this directory.
